 "wiki": {
  "title": "Glaucous-winged gull",
  "extract": "The glaucous-winged gull is a large, white-headed gull. The genus name is from Latin Larus which appears to have referred to a gull or other large seabird. The specific glaucescens is Neo-Latin for \"glaucous\" from the Ancient Greek, glaukos, denoting the grey color of its wings.",
